# A stored handset reads the List of Supported Lists (TS 102 527-3 §7.4.10)
# in a list access call, as the A540 does after a power cycle (its commands
# from the 2026-10-30 bench log), and releases the call.
# Identities, keys and numbers are made up.
sub 1 80 a8 03 11 22 33 44
start
ev hello api=N lines=1 hs=1
ev hs hs=1 state=registered name="DECT 1" wideband=1
mail 0153 00
mail 0169 07
mail 0157 00
mail 015b 01
mail 022c 01
mail 0247 02 00 00
mail 0247 03 00 00
mail 0247 04 00 00
mail 0247 05 00 00
mail 0247 06 00 00
mail fff1 07 18 95 00 00 11 00
mail fff1 07 29 95 00 00 11 00
mail fff1 07 3a 95 00 00 11 00
mail fff1 07 4b 95 00 00 11 00
mail fff1 07 5c 95 00 00 11 00
mail fff1 07 6d 95 00 00 11 00
mail 0247 01 01 00
mail 020a 01 b0 b1 b2 b3 b4 b5 b6 b7 b8 b9 ba bb bc bd be bf 00
mail fff1 07 18 95 00 00 11 00
mail 017c 00 01

up 1
# {CC-SETUP}, <<BASIC-SERVICE>> call class 2 (list access)
pp 03 05 05 07 80 a8 03 11 22 33 44 06 07 a0 a5 00 01 23 45 60 e0 28
fp 83 02
fp 05 40 0a 03 01 18 18 0c 08 db 00 25 4a 6f 94 b9 de 0e 08 03 28 4d 72 97 bc e1 06
tick 200
# {CC-IWU-INFO} <<IWU-TO-IWU>>: start session on list 00
pp 03 60 77 04 c3 00 00 00
fp 83 60 77 0a c3 01 00 81 81 00 00 00 ff 00
tick 200
# read entries: session 1, from entry 1, one entry, no mark, field 01
pp 03 60 77 07 c3 06 81 81 01 00 01
fp 83 60 77 05 c3 07 81 81 01
fp 83 60 77 11 c3 14 81 81 8c 01 8a 80 00 01 02 03 04 06 07 08 09
tick 200
# end session 1
pp 03 60 77 03 c3 02 81
fp 83 60 77 03 c3 03 81
tick 200
# {CC-RELEASE}, normal
pp 03 4d e2 00
fp 83 5a
tick 500
mail 0202 01
down
tick 1000
